    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">The new seam is exposed via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (interface `IActionSeam` + implementation, mirroring the existing facade pattern used by `IBriefingAi`/`BriefingAi`). Non-AI code (future Phase 4 comms-RI, Phase 5 suggestions) MUST consume the seam through this facade — never by injecting `CreateNotificationNodeExecutor`/`CreateTaskNodeExecutor`/`UpdateRecordNodeExecutor` directly, and never by constructing a `NodeExecutionContext` synthetically to satisfy the executor's existing signature.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not change the public constructor signature of `CreateNotificationNodeExecutor`, `CreateTaskNodeExecutor`, or `UpdateRecordNodeExecutor` in this task. Extract shared logic into new internal core class(es) that both the executor (via its own existing injected fields) and the new `IActionSeam` implementation (via its own separately-injected fields) call — never by adding a constructor parameter to the executors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Task 030's characterization tests (`tests/integration/seam/Ai/Nodes/*SeamTests.cs`) MUST pass with zero modifications after this task's refactor. `CreateTaskNodeExecutorTests.cs` and `UpdateRecordNodeExecutorTests.cs` MUST pass with zero modifications. If any of these tests requires an edit to keep passing, the extraction changed observable behavior — stop and re-derive the extraction, do not edit the tests to match (root §6).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope is strictly the THREE verified executors (`CreateNotification`, `CreateTask`, `UpdateRecord`) named in `plan.md`'s Reusable Code list. Do not invent a fourth "CreateEvent" node executor — no `CreateEvent*NodeExecutor.cs` exists under `Services/Ai/Nodes/` as of 2026-07-20 (verified: 18 executors total, none named CreateEvent). If a "Create Event" action is genuinely required by a later phase, that is a separate, explicitly-scoped decision for that phase's task, not this extraction.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Preserve the P5 ack-contract and `SurfaceLaunch`/dispatch entry points exactly as-is: do not touch `DispatchSessionEndpoint.cs`, `OutputRouter.cs`'s `SurfaceLaunch`/`Compose`/`Email`/`WorkProduct` cases, or `IUiActionAckCoordinator` in this task. This extraction is confined to `Services/Ai/Nodes/**` (internal refactor only) and new files under `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/**`. `DispositionRoutability.cs` and `OutputRouter.cs`'s `Notification` leg are task 033's concern, not this task's.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">The new seam-invokable-standalone proof is a `tests/integration/seam/**` test (not a `tests/unit/**` test) — it must demonstrate the seam works with NO `NodeExecutionContext`, NO playbook run, and NO chat session in scope, per FR-07's acceptance criterion.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/integration-tests.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>tests/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="ADR-013 facade pair" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IBriefingAi.cs + BriefingAi.cs">Interface + concrete implementation registered as the DI-visible surface; consumers outside `Services/Ai/` depend only on the interface. Follow this shape for `IActionSeam`/`ActionSeam`.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Existing static/near-static coercion helpers" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/UpdateRecordNodeExecutor.cs (CoerceFieldValue, CoerceStringMapping, CoerceChoiceFromMetadata — all already `NodeExecutionContext`-free)">These are the least-effort extraction target — they already take explicit parameters, not the execution context. Extracting `UpdateRecordAsync` is lower-risk than the Notification/Task legs.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Session-specific vs session-agnostic split" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/CreateNotificationNodeExecutor.cs BuildNotificationEntity">Template rendering + ConfigJson parsing (playbook-specific) stays IN the executor; the entity-building + idempotency-check + create call (session-agnostic) moves to the shared core. The executor renders templates from `NodeExecutionContext`, THEN calls the core with already-resolved plain values.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Run task 030's new seam tests and the existing `CreateTaskNodeExecutorTests.cs`/`UpdateRecordNodeExecutorTests.cs` to confirm the pre-extraction baseline is green.</step>
    <step order="2">Design and extract session-agnostic core logic: propose exact class/file names at task time (e.g. under a new `Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/` or `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` subfolder) for the Notification-create, Task-create, and UpdateRecord-update cores, each taking explicit typed parameters + the relevant Dataverse-boundary service instance (no `NodeExecutionContext`).</step>
    <step order="3">Refactor `CreateNotificationNodeExecutor`, `CreateTaskNodeExecutor`, `UpdateRecordNodeExecutor` to call the extracted core internally from their existing `ExecuteAsync` — keep template rendering + ConfigJson parsing in the executor; keep the executors' constructors, `Validate`, `SupportedExecutorTypes`, `GetConfigSchema`, and public `ExecuteAsync` signature unchanged.</step>
    <step order="4">Author `IActionSeam` (interface) and `ActionSeam` (implementation) under `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`, each of `CreateNotificationAsync`/`CreateTaskAsync`/`UpdateRecordAsync` calling the same extracted core with its own DI-injected Dataverse-boundary service instances. Register `IActionSeam`/`ActionSeam` in DI alongside the existing `PublicContracts` registrations (grep for the `IBriefingAi` registration site and mirror the convention).</step>
    <step order="5">Run task 030's characterization tests — confirm zero diffs required to pass. Run `CreateTaskNodeExecutorTests.cs`/`UpdateRecordNodeExecutorTests.cs` — confirm zero diffs required to pass.</step>
    <step order="6">Author a new `tests/integration/seam/Ai/PublicContracts/ActionSeamTests.cs` proving each `IActionSeam` method is invokable and produces a correct Dataverse write with NO `NodeExecutionContext`, playbook run, or chat session constructed anywhere in the test.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify BFF publish size + CVE scan per the standard BFF-touching-task checklist (no new package dependencies are expected for this task — confirm and report the delta as ~0 MB).</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to ✅ completed</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-notification-spine-r1/notes/</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If characterization tests (030) fail after extraction, STOP and escalate — do not adjust the tests to pass (root §6).</trigger>
    <trigger>If preserving `CreateTaskNodeExecutor`'s or `UpdateRecordNodeExecutor`'s exact existing constructor signature turns out to be structurally impossible without duplicating logic (defeating the extraction's purpose), STOP and escalate — this is a legitimate ADR-013/CLAUDE.md §11 tension (extend-vs-fork), not a case to silently resolve by breaking the "unmodified tests" acceptance criterion.</trigger>
  </escalation>

