  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the new `IActionSeam.CreateNotificationAsync`/`CreateTaskAsync`/`UpdateRecordAsync` methods, when invoked directly in a test with only a mocked Dataverse-boundary service (no `NodeExecutionContext`, no playbook run, no chat session), then each produces the same Dataverse write shape the corresponding node executor produces today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given task 030's characterization tests, when run against the post-extraction code, then they pass with ZERO source changes to the test files.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `CreateTaskNodeExecutorTests.cs` and `UpdateRecordNodeExecutorTests.cs`, when run against the post-extraction code, then they pass with ZERO source changes, including their existing constructor call signatures.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `CreateNotificationNodeExecutor`, `CreateTaskNodeExecutor`, `UpdateRecordNodeExecutor` public constructors, when compared before and after this task, then their parameter lists are byte-for-byte identical (diff shows no constructor signature change).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the `IActionSeam` interface, when grepped for consumers, then it is exposed ONLY under `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` and is the sole documented entry point for non-chat/non-playbook Layer-A record creation (ADR-013).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `DispatchSessionEndpoint.cs`, `OutputRouter.cs`, and `DispositionRoutability.cs`, when diffed after this task, then they are unchanged (this task does not touch the dispatch/router/registry surface — that is task 033's scope).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the negative case of an unresolvable required field (e.g., `CreateNotificationAsync` called with no recipientId and no fallback), when the seam method runs, then it returns a typed error/failure result rather than throwing an unhandled exception or silently no-op'ing — the seam's failure contract is at least as strict as the executor's today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish measured ≤60 MB compressed (report absolute + diff vs ~49.63 MB incl-PDB baseline, state PDB convention); 0 new HIGH CVE (`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`); Placement Justification stated per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` (new PublicContracts facade extends the existing `Services/Ai/` facade surface — no new package dependency expected).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec refs: FR-07, NFR-07. Plan refs: Phase 3 deliverables ("Layer-A seam invokable without a chat session or playbook run; existing executor tests pass unmodified"). The spec's phrase "Create Event/Task/Notification" is reconciled against the verified substrate as "Create Notification/Task/UpdateRecord" per plan.md's Reusable Code section — no CreateEvent executor exists; do not add one in this task.
  </notes>

